What is Buy Now, Pay Later?

What is BNPL?

BNPL or Buy Now Pay Later is the process through which a consumer acquires a good or service immediately and pays for it over time, usually in fixed instalments. In some ways it is a reverse lay-by system where the product or service is immediately accessible to the purchaser followed by the payments.

How does BNPL typically work?

Users of BNPL services will typically buy a product or service either online or in-store utilising the selected app of their service provider. This is then followed by an allocated time frame and a set number of periodic debits (usually every two weeks) until the purchase is paid off. The BNPL service provider usually collects a commission from the merchant in the range of 4-6% of the amount spent. Fees may be applied to late or overdue payments and these vary from provider to provider.


